OPTIONAL / RELATED (do not fold in unless the reviewer asks) — /workspace/src/data/helper/dataStackHelper.ts:205-209 has the identical falsy-name bug:

```ts
export function isDimensionStacked(data: SeriesData, stackedDim: string): boolean {
    return !!stackedDim && stackedDim === data.getCalculationInfo('stackedDimension');
}
```

When the stacked value dimension is named `''`, `getCalculationInfo('stackedDimension')` is also `''` (confirmed at runtime) yet `!!stackedDim` short-circuits to `false`, so `prepareDataCoordInfo` (`/workspace/src/chart/line/helper.ts:61-68`) reports `stacked: false` and the stacked area baseline falls back to `valueStart`. The safe equivalent is `stackedDim != null && stackedDim === data.getCalculationInfo('stackedDimension')` (when nothing is stacked `stackedDimension` is `undefined`, so `undefined != null` is `false` and behaviour is unchanged). This touches `src/layout/points.ts:51,54`, `src/layout/barGrid.ts:489`, `src/layout/barPolar.ts:104`, `src/component/marker/markerHelper.ts:65` and the public `echarts.helper.isDimensionStacked` export (`src/export/api/helper.ts:60`), so it is a wider blast radius than the stated acceptance signal.
